---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import type { Entry } from "../../lib/entries";
import cover from "./assets/door.png";

interface Props {
  entry: Entry;
}

const { entry } = Astro.props;
const { title, date, keywords } = entry.data;

const band =
  "px-(--gutter) py-(--pad) [--pad:clamp(120px,14vw,220px)] bg-linear-to-b/oklab";
const column = "mx-auto max-w-[34em] space-y-[1.1em] font-serif";
const large =
  "mx-auto mb-[clamp(56px,7vw,112px)] max-w-[12em] text-center font-serif text-[clamp(44px,7vw,132px)]/[1.04] tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance";
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description="Is escapism even bad? And how would you know if you were doing it?"
>
  <article class="overflow-x-clip">
    <div data-door class="peer relative h-dvh data-[walk=true]:h-[260dvh]">
      <div
        data-stage
        class="sticky top-0 h-dvh overflow-hidden paper [--box:max(110vw,154dvh)] [--open:0] [--shut:1]"
      >
        <p
          class="relative flex justify-between gap-6 px-(--gutter) pt-(--col-inset) font-mono text-[clamp(14px,1.1vw,18px)]/[2] text-muted"
        >
          <a
            class="text-charcoal link phone:inline-flex phone:min-h-11 phone:items-center"
            href="/index/"
          >
            $ cd ..
          </a>
          <span class="phone:hidden">
            <time datetime={date}>{date}</time>
            {` ${keywords.join(" ").toLowerCase()}`}
          </span>
        </p>

        <h1
          class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 grid grid-cols-[1fr_calc(var(--box)*0.23*var(--shut))_1fr] items-center gap-x-[clamp(16px,2vw,40px)] px-(--gutter) font-serif text-[min(calc(((100vw-var(--box)*0.23*var(--shut))/2-var(--gutter)-40px)/3.9),220px)]/[1] tracking-[-0.02em] [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:grid-cols-1 [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:grid-rows-[1fr_calc(var(--box)*0.326*var(--shut))_1fr] [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:gap-y-[clamp(20px,3vh,40px)] [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:text-center [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:text-[clamp(44px,12vw,120px)]"
        >
          <span
            class="text-right [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:self-end [@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:text-center"
            >Escapism</span
          >
          <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="[@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1)]:self-start"
            >as escapism</span
          >
        </h1>

        <img
          data-cover
          src={cover.src}
          width={cover.width}
          height={cover.height}
          alt="A lone door standing open in a dark field under a crescent moon. Through it, a road runs to the horizon and ends at another door."
          class="absolute top-[calc(50%-var(--box)*0.327)] left-[calc(50%-var(--box)*0.455)] w-(--box) max-w-none origin-[45.5%_49%] scale-[calc(var(--shut)+(1.1-var(--shut))*var(--open))] [clip-path:inset(calc(24.8%*(1-var(--open)))_calc(43.2%*(1-var(--open)))_calc(26.3%*(1-var(--open)))_calc(33.8%*(1-var(--open))))] [image-rendering:pixelated]"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section
      class:list={[
        band,
        "relative from-paper via-[#2a2a5e] via-[180px] to-[#4f458f] text-[clamp(21px,1.7vw,28px)]/[1.6] text-paper peer-data-[walk=true]:-mt-[60dvh] peer-data-[walk=true]:from-transparent peer-data-[walk=true]:via-[60dvh] peer-data-[walk=true]:pt-[calc(60dvh+clamp(40px,6vw,96px))]",
      ]}
    >
      <h2 class={large}>Is escapism even bad?</h2>
      <div class={column}>
        <p>
          I don’t know why we’re all so sure it is. Call something escapism and
          you’ve already said it’s a waste of time, even if you can’t say what
          the time was supposed to be for.
        </p>
        <p>
          Reading a novel all afternoon is fine. Playing a video game all
          afternoon is a problem. Both are hours spent somewhere other than your
          life, and I’ve never heard an explanation for the difference that
          wasn’t mostly about which one sounds better.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class:list={[
        band,
        "from-[#4f458f] to-[#8a4a8c] text-[clamp(21px,1.8vw,29px)]/[1.55] text-paper",
      ]}
    >
      <div class={column}>
        <p>
          The best test I have is what’s left afterward. Some things leave me
          clearer than I was. Others leave me numb, and I go back the next night
          anyway.
        </p>
        <p>
          The problem is I usually can’t tell until later, and sometimes not
          even then. The bad ones don’t feel bad while they’re happening. That’s
          more or less why people do them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class:list={[
        band,
        "from-[#8a4a8c] via-[#9a4f8e] via-[calc(100%-var(--pad))] to-[#bd6a81] text-[clamp(22px,1.9vw,30px)]/[1.55] text-paper",
      ]}
    >
      <div class={column}>
        <p>
          Some of it is plainly hiding. It’s not hard to call that self-care, or
          to leave every time things are about to get difficult and say you
          needed a break.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some of it might be the only reason a person gets through the week.
          From the outside those two look identical, and I’m not convinced they
          always feel different from the inside.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class:list={[
        band,
        "from-[#bd6a81] via-(length:--pad) via-[#f08a76] to-[#f1bdaf] text-[clamp(22px,2vw,31px)]/[1.5] text-charcoal",
      ]}
    >
      <div class={column}>
        <p>
          Maybe the word is covering at least three things: disappearing and
          feeling worse for it, stepping away and coming back better, and
          wandering off and finding something you weren’t looking for. Only the
          first one seems like a problem. I don’t know how reliably anyone can
          tell which one they’re doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class:list={[
        band,
        "from-[#f1bdaf] to-(length:--pad) to-paper text-[clamp(23px,2.1vw,33px)]/[1.5] text-charcoal",
      ]}
    >
      <div class={column}>
        <p>
          I used to feel guilty about any time that wasn’t getting me somewhere.
          I feel that less now, though I couldn’t tell you whether that’s
          because I figured something out or because I got better at excusing
          myself.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p
        class:list={[
          large,
          "mt-[clamp(72px,10vw,160px)] mb-[clamp(72px,10vw,160px)] max-w-[15em]",
        ]}
      >
        I can’t tell if this is a defense of escapism or just more of it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-center font-mono text-[clamp(14px,1.1vw,18px)]/[2]">
        <a
          class="link phone:inline-flex phone:min-h-11 phone:items-center"
          href="/index/"
        >
          $ cd ..
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { openDoorOnScroll } from "./components/door";
  import { paintScene } from "./components/scene";

  paintScene();
  openDoorOnScroll();
</script>
